(Compile-fail: bug #40 - `Write` hands its operand to FILE_WRITE_STR, which
 reads it as a pointer to text. A number holds a value, not an address, so
 writing one used 72 as an address and segfaulted the generated program.
 `Write` takes text, a buffer, or a format string; a scalar is refused here,
 the way `append` refuses one.)

open a file for writing called report at "/tmp/vox_write_number.txt".
a number called temperature is 72.
Write temperature to report.
close report.
